"# BMS / DJMax Keysound Slicer UX Audit\n\n**Research note.** This is an evidence-led audit, not a claim that every requested tool has public documentation. The Sayaslicer repository currently exposes six closed issues and no open-issue count; I found fewer than ten public issues, so I do not pad the requested “top 10” with guesses. PTSEQUENCER-specific 2047-limit documentation and usable Woslicer III guide text were not found in the fetched sources; those rows are explicitly marked unverified.\n\n## 1. Comparison table\n\n| Tool | Workflow | Top 3 pain points / limits evidenced by sources | Max slices / snap | Export method |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sayaslicer | Load audio; add markers; optionally import MIDI/Mid2BMS arrays or clipboard markers; preview; copy BMSE/iBMSC clipboard or export keysounds; save project. | Traditional file export remains available; iBMSC arbitrary-resolution markers can break BMS after zero-cross moves; very large files once failed; Linux preview once crashed. | Snap 1/1–1/192; arbitrary snapping; no published max slice count. | WAV keysound export, BMSE/iBMSC clipboard, keysound list/BMS append. [README](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) [issues](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/issues?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aclosed) |\n| Woslicer II | Prepare WAV; set BPM/start; click marker points on grid; use preview; “total output” writes numbered slices; use clipboard/definition workflow with BMSE. | Many manual clicks; separate definition and sequence-paste ceremony; tail/echo decisions are manual; output numbering/order must be kept aligned. | Guide documents arbitrary fine division but no numeric max; no 1/192 claim verified for Woslicer II. | Numbered WAV files plus clipboard/sequence information. [Japanese workflow](https://purureko.com/etc/post-1704/) [guide](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) |\n| Woslicer III | Drag WAV; set source start; place cuts on bar lines; preview between cuts; configure output/fade/noise gate; export WAV and WOS/clipboard sequence; define in BMSE. | A documented pop-noise mechanism exists around the slice tail; fade-before-cut shortens audio, fade-after-cut can leak the next sound; users must manually remove final empty slice and avoid long keysounds. | UI guide reports 3-digit names but says 4+ digits can be made; no snap denominator/max verified. | WAV files + WOS/clipboard sequence. [guide](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) [noise analysis](https://qiita.com/yuinore/items/79db943d2e3447adee71) |\n| BMHelper + Mid2BMS | MIDI/DAW render → generate split positions/temporary placement/definitions → Woslicer or Mid2BMS → paste definitions and sequence into BMSE; validate in player. | Clipboard paste can misplace objects; clipboard lifetime and insertion position matter; manual file/definition ordering and duplicate-definition cleanup are fragile. | BMHelper docs expose minimum interval, sorting, same-note tolerance, duplicate-definition interval and start number; no single max verified. | Generated WAVs, text/BMS definitions, clipboard sequence; later WAV→OGG conversion is separate. [BMHelper](https://w.atwiki.jp/coolnaurl/pages/19.html) [Mid2BMS workflow](https://trap.jp/post/777/) [iBMSC issue](https://github.com/zardoru/iBMSC/issues/5) |\n| PTSEQUENCER | No reliable public workflow/limit source was fetched. | The often-repeated “2047 keysound limit” was not verified as a PTSEQUENCER limit; do not implement it as fact. | Unverified. | Unverified. |\n| dtinth sound-slicer | Put source WAV/TXT in a project folder; tool slices WAV and creates BMS clipboard data; rhythmic or melodic `miditext` mode; paste into BMx Sequence Editor. | Rhythmic mode can create 1,000 slices from 1,000 notes and slight gaps; melodic mode requires render MIDI back to WAV and then slice; both modes do not support BPM changes. | No max; no snap UI. | WAV slices + BMS clipboard. [README](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) |\n| FL Studio + Mid2BMS | Protect/copy FL project; export MIDI; create/render channel WAV(s); configure Mid2BMS array/base paths; run slice; rename/assemble definitions; convert WAV to OGG separately; validate. | Accidental overwrite can be “a disaster”; automation/low-volume material may fail in normal mode; single-WAV red-mode exports can become too large. | No slicer max/snap claim verified. | Many WAVs, generated BMS definitions, optional batch WAV→OGG. [workflow](https://trap.jp/post/777/) |\n\n## 2. Problem inventory\n\n### Timeline\n\n| Severity | Problem / limit | Evidence and UX implication |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Time-domain cuts and chart-domain placement are separate artifacts. BMHelper copies marker positions to Woslicer, then sequence data is pasted into BMSE; a misplaced start position can shift the entire import. | The documented workflow requires repeated copy/paste and warns about start position/order. A dual ruler with linked chart preview would remove this class of error. [BMHelper](https://w.atwiki.jp/coolnaurl/pages/19.html) [workflow](https://purureko.com/etc/post-1704/) |\n| P0 | Tail handling is musically consequential: fading before a cut shortens a sound; fading after can include the next sound. | Woslicer III analysis explicitly describes both failure modes. Use virtual endMs plus preview, not destructive tail surgery. [Qiita](https://qiita.com/yuinore/items/79db943d2e3447adee71) |\n| P1 | Grid/BPM assumptions fail on tempo changes. | dtinth’s README states both modes do not support BPM changes; Sayaslicer calls BPM-change support partial/hackish and lists better BPM support as planned. [sound-slicer](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) |\n| P1 | Fine-resolution placement is unsafe when audio cleanup moves markers. | Sayaslicer warns zero-crossing moves markers and can make iBMSC data invalid; BMSE mode rounds to nearest 192nd. [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) |\n| P2 | Older workflows lack a chart-aware “play this slice in context” loop. | Woslicer’s documented preview is interval-based, while the sequence is pasted later into BMSE. [Wix guide](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) |\n\n### Interface\n\n| Severity | Problem / limit | Evidence and recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Export/definition ceremony creates alignment risk: filenames, Explorer sort order, definition start index, paste origin and lane must agree. | The tutorial explicitly warns that Explorer ordering and selected start positions determine definitions; another warns to reload if the wrong file is dragged first. [purureko](https://purureko.com/etc/post-1704/) [Wix](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) |\n| P1 | Clipboard is a hidden transport layer with surprising state. | BMHelper clipboard data disappears when BMHelper closes; its early “copy definitions” had a no-newline defect; iBMSC reported BMSE clipboard data pasting incorrectly. [BMHelper](https://w.atwiki.jp/coolnaurl/pages/19.html) [iBMSC #5](https://github.com/zardoru/iBMSC/issues/5) |\n| P1 | File-list management is the real cost of slicing. | sound-slicer’s example project contains one source plus numbered WAVs; rhythmic mode can produce one slice per note; tutorials require folder assembly and cleanup. [sound-slicer](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) [trap.jp](https://trap.jp/post/777/) |\n| P2 | Accessibility/portability issues require user intervention. | Sayaslicer release notes mention unsigned macOS installation; closed issues include macOS launch, Linux preview/PortAudio, text enlargement, and >2GB loading. [releases](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/releases) [issues](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/issues?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aclosed) |\n\n### Settings\n\n| Severity | Problem / limit | Evidence and recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | “Zero-crossing” is not universally safe: it reduces clicks but changes chart timing at arbitrary resolution. | Sayaslicer documents the tradeoff; Woslicer III’s pop analysis shows why endpoint processing needs preview and per-slice override. [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) [Qiita](https://qiita.com/yuinore/items/79db943d2e3447adee71) |\n| P1 | Tail/noise controls are coupled to musical intent. | Woslicer III exposes fade/reverse-tail/noise-gate concepts; BMHelper exposes minimum interval and duplicate-definition interval, which affect whether tails are retained or sounds are reused. [Wix](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) [BMHelper](https://w.atwiki.jp/coolnaurl/pages/19.html) |\n| P1 | One global normalization/cleanup policy is inappropriate for mixed material. | The workflows distinguish low-volume/automation material and recommend Edison/manual slicing when automatic slicing fails. [trap.jp](https://trap.jp/post/777/) |\n| P2 | Users need discoverable shortcuts, not only mouse placement. | Sayaslicer documents marker, preview, snap, copy/export, selection and undo shortcuts; Woslicer II is described as having extensive keyboard shortcuts. [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) [Mid2BMS wiki](https://wiki.mid2bms.net/%E4%BB%96%E3%83%84%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AB/woslicer) |\n\n### Backend / interchange\n\n| Severity | Problem / limit | Evidence and recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Destructive export makes correction expensive and creates hundreds of assets. | sound-slicer’s project layout and rhythmic mode demonstrate the asset explosion; Mid2BMS requires generated WAVs, renamed folders and later conversion. [sound-slicer](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) [trap.jp](https://trap.jp/post/777/) |\n| P0 | BMS identifier-space overflow/definition pressure is operational, even where a numeric PTSEQUENCER limit is not proven. | A tutorial warns definitions must not pass `#WAVZZ` and recommends BGM routing or reusing identical sounds. [Wix](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) |\n| P1 | Long individual keysounds can cause playback/format problems. | The guide warns not to leave a key over one minute and recommends about 50 seconds; this is a BMS-tooling constraint, not a universal audio limit. [Wix](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) |\n| P1 | Round-trip fidelity differs by clipboard format. | Sayaslicer says BMSE clipboard rounds to 192nd, while iBMSC supports arbitrary maximum resolution but can fail after zero-cross movement. [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) |\n| P1 | Stereo/non-stereo and very large-file handling have been real implementation edges. | Sayaslicer release notes record a non-stereo waveform fix; closed issue #5 records >2GB load failure. [releases](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/releases) [issue list](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/issues?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aclosed) |\n\n## 3. What Sayaslicer did right vs Woslicer — keep these\n\n**Keep from Sayaslicer:** cross-platform distribution; drag/drop; project save/load; arbitrary 1/1–1/192 snap; BMSE and iBMSC clipboard paths; Base-62 toggle; MIDI and Mid2BMS imports; keysound-list export; copy/paste markers; undo/redo; configurable silent-tail removal, fade and zero-crossing; marker-list navigation; and keyboard-first preview/marker movement. These are all explicitly listed or documented in its README/release notes. [README](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) [release](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/releases)\n\n**Keep from Woslicer:** the very direct “waveform → marker → interval preview → output” mental model; fast keyboard shortcuts; BPM/grid-oriented cutting; and explicit controls for tail extension, fade and noise gate. The user guides show that this simple loop is still effective for non-MIDI/automation material. [Woslicer workflow](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) [Mid2BMS wiki](https://wiki.mid2bms.net/%E4%BB%96%E3%83%84%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AB/woslicer)\n\n## 4. Top 10 recommendations for DJMax Studio\n\n1. **P0 — Make virtual slices first-class objects**: `{sourceFile,startMs,endMs}` with non-destructive edits and export only on finalize. This directly removes the numbered-WAV/folder-management burden documented by sound-slicer and Mid2BMS. [sound-slicer](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) [trap.jp](https://trap.jp/post/777/)\n2. **P0 — Ship the proposed dual timeline**: waveform bottom, Studio chart preview top, shared playhead, beat/bar and millisecond rulers. Existing workflows split marker copy from chart placement and therefore expose paste-origin errors. [BMHelper](https://w.atwiki.jp/coolnaurl/pages/19.html)\n3. **P0 — Add “Import to Studio” and round-trip metadata**: never require clipboard as the primary integration; preserve source IDs, start/end, lane, quantization and overrides. Clipboard defects and format-specific rounding are documented. [iBMSC #5](https://github.com/zardoru/iBMSC/issues/5) [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer)\n4. **P0 — Per-slice endpoint safety controls**: Zero-X on/off, fade shape/length, tail policy, preview-before/after, and a visual warning when the endpoint moves off the grid. This addresses both Woslicer pop/tail failure modes and Sayaslicer’s zero-cross/iBMSC warning. [Qiita](https://qiita.com/yuinore/items/79db943d2e3447adee71) [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer)\n5. **P1 — Snap from 1/4 through 1/192 plus arbitrary millisecond mode**, with explicit quantization preview and resnap-all. Sayaslicer proves demand for arbitrary snap and resnap; BMSE interchange proves 192nd is a practical compatibility boundary. [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer)\n6. **P1 — BPM-map-aware grid with a visible “hack/unsupported” state**. Older tools either do not support BPM changes or call support partial/hackish. [sound-slicer](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer)\n7. **P1 — Slice Library with deduplication and reuse**: show source, duration, hash/similarity, use count, and “reuse this slice.” The ecosystem explicitly reduces 500 events to 10 reusable slices in melodic mode and recommends reuse to avoid `#WAVZZ` pressure. [sound-slicer](https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer) [Wix](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3)\n8. **P1 — Draft slice and reversible preview**: preview in chart context, audition tail, and commit only when accepted. This replaces destructive “export, import, discover pop, redo” loops evidenced by Woslicer III analysis. [Qiita](https://qiita.com/yuinore/items/79db943d2e3447adee71)\n9. **P1 — Explicit format/mode switcher (BMS / RESPECT / TECHNIKA)** with validation rules and export reports. Do not silently assume BMS identifier/lane semantics; the NamuWiki reference describes DJMAX key sounds, licensing/keyless cases, and different game behavior. [NamuWiki](https://en.namu.wiki/w/%ED%82%A4%EC%9D%8C)\n10. **P2 — Power-user command system and diagnostics**: preserve Sayaslicer’s shortcuts, add searchable actions, and provide a preflight report for overlap, missing source, >1-minute slices, grid drift, duplicate/overflow risk, clipping and stereo/format compatibility. The need is grounded in the documented manual checks and known implementation edges. [sayaslicer](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer) [Wix](https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3) [releases](https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/releases)\n\n## 5. Raw source list\n\n- https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer\n- https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/issues?q=is%3Aissue+state%3Aclosed\n- https://github.com/SayakaIsBaka/sayaslicer/releases\n- https://purureko.com/etc/post-1704/\n- https://w.atwiki.jp/coolnaurl/pages/19.html\n- https://qiita.com/yuinore/items/79db943d2e3447adee71\n- https://wiki.mid2bms.net/%E4%BB%96%E3%83%84%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AB/woslicer\n- https://spirea3cross.wixsite.com/bmstukuru2020/how-to-make3\n- https://trap.jp/post/777/\n- https://github.com/zardoru/iBMSC/issues/5\n- https://github.com/dtinth/sound-slicer\n- https://en.namu.wiki/w/%ED%82%A4%EC%9D%8C\n- https://note.com/tiv_03sk/n/n97ce18606798\n- https://github.com/BMS-Community/resources\n\n## Evidence gaps\n\nI did not find a fetched public source that substantiates a PTSEQUENCER-specific 2047 limit, a complete Woslicer III shortcut/settings reference, or accessible YouTube comments for these tools. Those items are intentionally not stated as facts. Likewise, no Sayaslicer label-filtered “top 10” exists in the fetched issue inventory; the public closed list contains six issues.\n"